  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 124 PM CDT Fri Jul 24 2026\n\nA high pressure will continue to build over South Texas into next\nweek leading to a more typical hot summer pattern. In addition,\ndry air in the mid-upper levels (700-300mb) will prohibit\nprecipitation and mid-level cloud cover leading to mostly sunny \nand clear conditions. Starting Sunday, dew point temperatures will\nrise, leading to an increased heat risk for the area. Overall, \nthere will be a moderate heat risk through early next week across \nthe CWA with western locations under a major heat risk. An extreme\nheat risk is in play for the brush country starting mid to late \nweek.",
